    m_Localized: ' Disclaimer'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 108754519281115136
    m_Localized: "Bibliograf\xEDa general consultada en el estudio de correcci\xF3n,
      validaci\xF3n y adiciones al guion del tour virtual 360\xB0 al Palacio de Carondelet:"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 108754544929284096
    m_Localized: 'Con el apoyo de:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 108754609223770112
    m_Localized: "Validaci\xF3n de textos hist\xF3ricos:"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 108754949654454272
    m_Localized: 'Desarrollo:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 126823099914526720
    m_Localized: "Usa el teclado para navegar \nPara desactivar el modo accesible
      presiona \u201CTab\u201D "
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 126823290252042240
    m_Localized: "The present digital platform has been developed as an institutional,
      educational, and cultural initiative aimed at promoting, preserving, and disseminating
      the historical and cultural heritage of the Palacio de Carondelet.\n\n<b>1.
      Scope of Virtual Reconstructions</b>\nThe virtual recreations and tours constitute
      digital representations developed from historical information, graphic records,
      and specialized technical criteria. Consequently, they may present variations
      in details, proportions, colors, textures, and lighting compared to the actual
      physical spaces.\n\nThese recreations do not replace the in-person experience,
      nor do they constitute an exact or definitive representation of the building.
      As technological interpretations of a heritage site, they may partially differ
      from the physical visit, and such differences shall not generate institutional
      liability.\n\n<b>2. Historical and Interpretative Content</b>\nThe historical
      narratives included in the tour are based on historiographical criteria and
      the availability of documentary sources and therefore constitute informed interpretations.\n\nThe
      information displayed on the plaques accompanying the presidential portraits
      corresponds to the data contained in the original objects exhibited in the
      Hall of Presidents.\n\n<b>3. Collaborations and Specific Content</b>\nThe exhibition
      \u201CD\xEDas de la Patria\u201D is a collaborative initiative of the Records
      and Archives Management Directorate of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and
      Human Mobility.\n\n<b>Some of the works located in the Cabinet Hall and the
      Oratory belong to the National Collection of Ecuador, under the Ministry of
      Education, Sports and Culture.</b>\n\nIn addition, part of the artworks displayed
      in the Banquet Hall belong to the Alberto Mena Caama\xF1o Reserve Collection
      of the Metropolitan Cultural Center of Quito.\n\nThe written translation into
      the Kichwa language has been prepared in Kichwa Unificado; the audio performances
      of the Baron of Carondelet were interpreted in the Otavalo Kichwa dialect.
      The English and French interpretations were performed by native speakers.\n\n<b>4.
      Technical Requirements and Functionality</b>\nThe 3D experience of this virtual
      tour requires a minimum level of technical performance. Therefore, optimal
      operation cannot be guaranteed on devices that do not meet the following specifications:\n\n<b>Mobile
      Phones</b>\n\u2022 Mid-range or higher smartphone (released within the last
      3\u20134 years). \n\u2022 4 GB RAM or higher. \n\u2022 64 GB storage or higher.
      \n\u2022 Android 13 or later / iPhone with iOS 15 or later. \n\u2022 Updated
      browser (Chrome, Safari, or another modern browser). \n\u2022 Stable 4G or
      Wi-Fi internet connection. \n\n<b>Computers (PC or Mac)</b>\n\u2022 Modern
      processor (equivalent to Intel Core i5 or AMD Ryzen 5 and above). \n\u2022
      16 GB RAM. \n\u2022 512 GB SSD or higher. \n\u2022 Windows 11, macOS Monterey
      (12) or later, or updated Linux distribution. \n\u2022 Updated browser (Chrome,
      Edge, Firefox, or Safari). \n\u2022 Stable internet connection (Wi-Fi or wired).
      \n\n<b>Tablets</b>\n\u2022 Mid-range or higher tablet. \n\u2022  4 GB RAM or
      higher. \n\u2022  64 GB storage or higher. \n\u2022  Android 12+, iPadOS 15+,
      or equivalent updated operating system. \n\u2022  Updated modern browser. \n\u2022 
      Stable Wi-Fi connection (LTE/5G optional). \n\nDisplay quality (including colors,
      resolution, and contrast) may vary depending on the device used.\n\nUsers are
      advised to navigate the platform using a mouse, as it provides more precise
      and fluid interaction within the three-dimensional environments. When using
      a laptop trackpad, functionality may vary depending on the model, sensitivity,
      device settings, and browser used.\n\n<b>5. User Responsibility and Limitations</b>\nAccess
      to and use of the virtual tour are undertaken at the sole responsibility of
      the user. The institution shall not be held liable for service interruptions,
      technical failures, incompatibility with devices, browsers, or operating systems,
      nor for any direct or indirect damages arising from the use of the platform.\n\n<b>6.
      Intellectual Property</b>\nAll contents of the virtual tour are protected under
      applicable intellectual property and copyright laws. Reproduction, distribution,
      or commercial use without the express authorization of the institution is strictly
      prohibited.\n\n<b>7. Content Updates</b>\nThe content presented \u2014 including
      texts, images, audio, videos, 3D models, and interactive resources \u2014 is
      provided for reference purposes only and may be subject to updates, technical
      adjustments, or interpretative modifications without prior notice.\n\nThe institution
      does not guarantee the absolute accuracy, completeness, or permanent timeliness
      of the published information."
